# Jest / Heft Testing (Awesome-adapted · SPFx)

Runner: `npm test` → `heft test`. Match existing `describe` / `it` style in `src/webparts/trcHome/**/*.test.ts`.

## TDD gate (bugfix / new logic)
- Write the failing test first, run it, confirm it fails for the right reason — only then write the fix/implementation
- If a test can't be run to watch it fail first (e.g. rig limitation), say so explicitly instead of skipping the gate silently

## Focus
- Business logic, pure utils, rule evaluators, services — not DOM canvas pixels
- Mock SharePoint/PnP/Graph **before** imports when needed (`jest.mock`)
- Valid · invalid · edge (empty, null, boundary, thrown errors)

## Practices
- Descriptive `it('should …')` names
- Group with `describe` per module/behavior
- `beforeEach` → `jest.clearAllMocks()` when mocks used
- 3–5 focused cases per file unless domain needs more (follow neighbor test files)
- Deterministic: stub dates via existing test helpers (e.g. `setSearchOverrideForTests`) — no real network

## SPFx specifics
- No full web part mount unless project already does — prefer pure function tests
- Do not import `@microsoft/sp-*` in tests without rig mocks
- Fluent UI components: test behavior via props/callbacks, not full theme tree

## Reject
- Snapshot-only tests for logic
- Adding Vitest/Playwright/Cypress for unit tests without user ask
- Tests that log tokens/PII
